{
  "name": "plate-25-mesh-backlash-ladder",
  "version_tag": "#116 mesh backlash ladder \u2014 the #115 coupon meshed but BOUND. Root cause: the profile shift blew the sun tooth to 4.28mm at pitch (fatter than nominal 3.93) so FDM swell had no room. Fix: DROP the shift (clean stub involute x=0 \u2014 this mesh only ORIENTS, no torque, so tooth strength is moot) + open backlash. 3 mesh pairs (7t sun + 12t receiver) at backlash 0.5/0.9/1.3, clean involute, gear bores opened to 2.80 so post friction can't fake a mesh bind. Spin each labeled pair (05/09/13 on the receiver, last digit on the sun; base labels each post pair); first that rolls free wins -> lock that backlash into the real sun tower + receiver laminae. All flat, no supports. xy_contour_compensation -0.06. | QUIET.",
